  "notes": "{傾|かし}げる almost always appears in the set expression ⟦{首|くび}→首：00792_kubi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{傾|かし}げる (to tilt one's head), a gesture of puzzlement or doubt — for humans and animals alike.\n\nWRITING: Related to ⟦{傾|かたむ}く→傾く：00200_katamuku⟧ (to lean); an alternative, less common reading is {傾|かた}げる.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{不思議|ふしぎ}→不思議：02358_fushigi⟧そう⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{首|くび}→首：00792_kubi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{傾|かし}げる: to tilt one's head as if puzzled\n- ⟦{疑問|ぎもん}→疑問：02648_gimon⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{感|かん}じて→感じる：02044_kanjiru⟧⟦{首|くび}→首：00792_kubi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{傾|かし}げる: to tilt one's head in doubt\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {傾|かし}げる: almost always the head (⟦{首|くび}→首：00792_kubi⟧), an expressive gesture\n- ⟦{傾|かたむ}ける→傾ける：11516_katamukeru⟧: general tilting of objects, not the head-tilt gesture\n- ⟦{傾|かたむ}く→傾く：00200_katamuku⟧: intransitive, the thing itself leans\n\nREGISTER: Neutral; common in both speech and writing.",
